<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ubashi Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ubashi Khan was the last khan of the Kalmyk Khanate on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>, ruling from 1761. Resenting Russian settlement, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> encroachment and interference in Kalmyk affairs, in January 1771 he led about 150,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmyks">Kalmyks</a> east across the Kazakh steppe towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a>. Many died from attacks, cold and hunger, and the survivors settled under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> then abolished the khanate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ubashi-khan.jpg" alt="Ubashi Khan" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Denis Attiret · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ubasi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
